<!DOCTYPE node PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD D-Bus Object Introspection 1.0//EN"
 "https://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/introspect.dtd">
<node name="/com/lantharos/Firewall1">
  <!--
    Luft's firewall. Every Wi-Fi and wired network is home or public, kept as the
    NetworkManager connection's connection.zone ("home" or "public"); one nobody chose yet
    counts as public. Devices on a network reach only the apps allowed there.

    An app is ("app", app id) for Flatpaks and apps started from a desktop file, or
    ("program", name) for programs that run outside an app, such as ones started in a terminal.
    Every person on the computer has their own choices: a call changes the caller's.

    Unclassified: the networks in use that nobody chose a type for yet, as (connection, name),
    connection being the NetworkManager settings path.
    HomeInterfaces: the network interfaces that are on a home network right now, by name, such
    as "wlan0". Anything that should only look for or show itself to devices at home, such as
    printer discovery and Post, follows this instead of reading the networks itself.
    OpenPorts: ports opened for services that run without an app, as (port, protocol, networks),
    protocol being "tcp" or "udp" and networks "home" for home networks only or "anywhere" for
    every network.
    Apps: what each app the firewall was told about may do, as (kind, id, access, uid): "home"
    lets devices on home networks connect, "anywhere" also devices on public networks, "blocked"
    none; uid is the user who chose.
    Waiting: apps listening for connections from the network that their user didn't decide about
    yet, as (kind, id, uid), uid being the user running the app. Empty while only public networks
    are connected.

    SetNetworkType sets a connection's type to "home" or "public", SetAppAccess what an app of
    the caller's may do and ForgetApp forgets that again, so the app is asked about the next time
    it listens. Making a network home and letting devices connect to an app ask the person at
    the computer to confirm with their password or fingerprint, so callers allow the prompt;
    letting devices on public networks connect needs an administrator. Making a network public,
    blocking an app and forgetting one don't ask. OpenPort and ClosePort need an administrator.
    Every prompt says what is about to change. SetExtensionPorts is for Kestrel:
    it opens the ports its extensions listen on, on home networks, for Kestrel alone, and asks
    the person to confirm a port the first time it is named. SetPostOpen is
    for Post, Kestrel's way of sending files to devices nearby: it opens LocalSend's port 53317 on
    home networks while someone may find the computer. Both are refused unless the caller runs
    in its own unit of the desktop, kestrel.service and kestrel-post.service.
  -->
  <interface name="com.lantharos.Firewall1">
    <property name="Unclassified" type="a(os)" access="read"/>
    <property name="HomeInterfaces" type="as" access="read"/>
    <property name="OpenPorts" type="a(qss)" access="read"/>
    <property name="Apps" type="a(sssu)" access="read"/>
    <property name="Waiting" type="a(ssu)" access="read"/>
    <method name="SetNetworkType">
      <arg name="network" type="o" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="kind" type="s" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <method name="OpenPort">
      <arg name="port" type="q" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="protocol" type="s" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="networks" type="s" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <method name="ClosePort">
      <arg name="port" type="q" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="protocol" type="s" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <method name="SetAppAccess">
      <arg name="kind" type="s" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="id" type="s" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="access" type="s" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <method name="ForgetApp">
      <arg name="kind" type="s" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="id" type="s" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <method name="SetPostOpen">
      <arg name="open" type="b" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <method name="SetExtensionPorts">
      <arg name="ports" type="a(qs)" direction="in"/>
    </method>
  </interface>
</node>
